<!--
    Swift standard-library C entry points.

    Issue: the standard library's own C entry points (`_swift_stdlib_*`)
    carried no signature, so a caller's live floating-point registers became
    the first arguments of `_swift_stdlib_reportUnimplementedInitializer`
    (`(x, y, width, height, "Frame", 5, "init(frame:)", 0xc, 0)`) and the
    version triple `_swift_stdlib_operatingSystemVersion` returns through
    `x8` read as an untyped stack array.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement, `SwiftRuntimePass`
    (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/swift/kuna_swiftruntime.rs`). No option: the
    signatures are the shims headers' (`AssertionReporting.h`,
    `FoundationShims.h`), like the rest of the table.

    The fixture `swift_stdlib_macho` (arm64 Mach-O, assembled from
    `swift_stdlib_macho.s` against the iOS 16.5 libswiftCore) reports an
    unimplemented initializer from `report_rect`, whose declared rectangle
    rides in `d0`..`d3` and is otherwise unused, and reads the major version
    off the triple in `os_major`. `try_value` is a `try!` that fails into
    `swift_unexpectedError` (`SWIFT_NORETURN` in `swift/Runtime/Error.h`),
    with a `return 7` after the call that is never reached; `free_box_scaled`
    deallocates a box with a double live across `swift_deallocBox`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
